# BreatheAI — Environment Variables Reference

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values.
**Never commit `.env` to version control.**

```dotenv
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  REQUIRED — Minimum configuration to run the application
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# WAQI Air Quality API Token
# Used for: ground-station AQI data feed + map tile overlays
# Get a free token at: https://aqicn.org/data-platform/token/
VITE_WAQI_TOKEN=

# Google Gemini API Key
# Used for: AI conversational assistant (Tier 2 browser fallback)
# Get a free key at: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Groq Cloud API Keys
# Used for: AI conversational assistant (Tier 1 — fastest inference)
# Get a free key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_LLM_API_KEY=        # server-side only (Vite proxy + serverless functions)
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=       # client-side direct browser fetch fallback

# Supabase Project
# Used for: saved locations, AQI alerts, community reports
# Falls back to localStorage automatically when not configured.
# Create a free project at: https://supabase.com/dashboard
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OPTIONAL — Ollama Fallback Safety (AI Tier 3)
#  Route AI through https://ollama.com/v1
#  Note: Ollama's /v1 endpoint blocks browser CORS preflight.
#  It is only reached via the serverless proxy or Vite dev proxy.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# VITE_OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
# VITE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
# OLLAMA_MODEL=deepseek-v4.1-flash
# VITE_OLLAMA_MODEL=deepseek-v4.1-flash

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OPTIONAL — Custom Llama / OpenAI-compatible LLM (AI Tier 4)
#  Supports: Groq, Together AI, OpenRouter, Cerebras, Fireworks, etc.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# VITE_LLAMA_API_KEY=
# VITE_LLAMA_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# VITE_LLAMA_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SMTP Configuration for Smart AQI Email Alerts (Server-Side Only)
#  Never expose SMTP password to client. Handled strictly by /api/send-alert-email
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SMTP_HOST=mail.yourdomain.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_SECURE=true
SMTP_USER=no-reply@yourdomain.com
SMTP_PASS=your_smtp_password
SMTP_FROM="BreatheAI Alerts <no-reply@yourdomain.com>"
```

## Security notes

| Variable | Exposed to browser bundle? | Risk |
|----------|---------------------------|------|
| `SMTP_*` | ❌ No (server-side only) | Low — credentials never sent to browser |
| `VITE_WAQI_TOKEN` | ✅ Yes | Low — WAQI keys are domain-restricted |
| `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY` | ✅ Yes | Medium — rate-limited by Google |
| `VITE_GROQ_API_KEY` | ✅ Yes | Medium — free-tier rate-limited |
| `GROQ_LLM_API_KEY` | ❌ No (server-side only) | Low — never sent to browser |
| `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | ✅ Yes | Low — anon key is designed to be public; protect via Supabase RLS policies |
| `OLLAMA_API_KEY` | ❌ No | None |
| `VITE_OLLAMA_API_KEY` | ✅ Yes (but CORS-blocked in browser) | Very low |

**Production recommendation:** Disable all `VITE_` AI keys in production and route 100% of AI traffic through the serverless `/api/breathe-ai` endpoint using only the server-side `GROQ_LLM_API_KEY`.
